1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,530
DIMNA: Psst! Hey, you! Yes, you! Want to hear a story?

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:10,020
KALILA: Dimna, you can't just jump out of bushes. Introduce us first!

3
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:14,660
DIMNA: Oh, right. I'm Dimna, the clever one. And this is my big brother, Kalila...

4
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:16,350
KALILA: ...the wise one.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:22,330
KALILA: We are two jackals from a very, very old book. It's called Kalila and Dimna.

6
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,110
DIMNA: Named after us, of course.

7
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:35,000
About two thousand years ago, wise storytellers in India wrote animal stories, to teach young princes how to live wisely.

8
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:42,130
Then a Persian doctor named Borzuy traveled all the way to India, to bring the stories home to Persia.

9
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:50,580
From Persia, the stories flew to the whole world. Into Arabic, Persian, Hebrew, Latin, Spanish, and many more languages.

10
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:56,460
DIMNA: We're famous! We're basically the oldest cartoon stars in the world.

11
00:00:56,610 --> 00:01:00,270
KALILA: There were no cartoons two thousand years ago, Dimna.

12
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:07,820
KALILA: Inside the book live clever hares, silly monkeys, brave mice, and proud lions.

13
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:11,860
DIMNA: And every story hides a secret. A little piece of wisdom!

14
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:16,560
KALILA: Like being kind, being a good friend, and thinking before you act.

15
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:22,110
KALILA: Every week, we'll bring you a new story from this old book.

16
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:27,490
DIMNA: And our first one is about a tiny hare, and a very, very big lion. Guess who wins!

17
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:31,110
KALILA: Come and listen. Old stories, for new friends.

